EarthJev reformats benchmark rows and prompts, adds spatial cues to selected questions,
and records model outputs. The split, calibration, reference and test rows retain their
respective benchmark terms. Source imagery retains its original terms, including FAIR1M,
GLH-Bridge and STAR for LRS-VQA, and DOTA (academic use), ITCVD (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0),
MiniFrance/HRSCD (IGN licence ouverte) and ISPRS Toronto/Potsdam (research use,
no redistribution) for XLRS.
